<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.4.5: Perfect Square and Squared Factors</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02395</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.4.5: Perfect Square and Squared Factors</md:title>
    <md:uuid>31f90e7b-32d1-4626-a1db-aaf001591f7f</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001">
    <section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00002">
      <title>Cool Down Activity</title>
      <exercise id="_40d670be-9621-4051-b6fe-46dc38a51273" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00001"><para id="para-00001">Enter the value of \(c\).</para><para id="para-00002">Answer the following questions for expression \(4x^2−28x+c\).</para>
      <para id="para-00003">Find the value of \(c\) to make the expression a perfect square.</para>
      </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">Correct! 49. Standard form: \(4x^2−28x+49\).</para>
          <para id="para-00005">The correct answer is 49. Standard form: \(4x^2−28x+49\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
    <example id="exam-00001"><exercise>
  <problem id="prob-00002">
    
    <para id="para-00006">Write an equivalent expression in the form of squared factors.</para>
    <para id="para-00007">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution id="sol-00002">
  <para id="para-00008">Compare your answer:</para>
  
  <para id="para-00009">Squared factors: \((2x−7)^2\).</para>

</solution></exercise>
</example>
    <example id="exam-00002"><exercise>
  <problem id="prob-00003">
    
    <para id="para-00010">Solve the equation \(4x^2−28x=-33\) by completing the square. Show your reasoning.</para>
    <para id="para-00011">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution id="sol-00003">
  <para id="para-00012">Compare your answer:</para>
  
  <para id="para-00013">\(\begin{aligned} 4 x^{2}-28 x &amp;=-33 \\ 4 x^{2}-28 x+49 &amp;=-33+49 \\ (2 x-7)^{2} &amp;=16 \\ \sqrt{(2 x-7)^{2}} &amp;=\sqrt{16} \\ 2 x-7 &amp;=4 \\ 2 x-7 &amp;=-4 \\ 2 x &amp;=11 \\ 2 x &amp;=3 \end{aligned}\)</para>
  
  <para id="para-00014"> \(x=\frac{11}{2} \text { and } x=\frac{3}{2}\) </para>

</solution></exercise>
</example>
  </section>
</content>
